# nr-office-ooxml-validator: integration fragment

New module `ooxml_validator` of the crate mixdog-ooxml (Open XML SDK validator launcher: npm tarball download, integrity,
unpack, cache lock, spawn). No protocol method, service or SERVICE_PENDING name belongs to it. The binary stays the external
npm package binary; nothing is bundled.

## native/core/Cargo.toml, [workspace.dependencies]

Add (beside flate2):

    tar = { version = "0.4.45", default-features = false } # the validator tarball's reader; its dependencies filetime and libc are in Cargo.lock already (xattr is the default feature and is not wanted)

## native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml/Cargo.toml (file of nr-office-ooxml-package; edit as the lead merges)

[dependencies], add:

    base64 = { workspace = true }
    flate2 = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-rt = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-statefile = { workspace = true }
    reqwest = { workspace = true }
    tar = { workspace = true }
    tokio = { workspace = true, features = ["rt", "time", "net", "process", "io-util"] }

(already there: mixdog-fsio, mixdog-js, serde_json, sha2.) `base64` moves from [dev-dependencies] to [dependencies].

[dev-dependencies], add:

    flate2 = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-rt = { workspace = true, features = ["test-support"] }
    tar = { workspace = true }
    tokio = { workspace = true, features = ["rt"] }

## native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml/src/lib.rs (file of nr-office-ooxml-package)

Add `pub mod ooxml_validator;` (alphabetical, after `opc`) and, in the module list sentence of the crate doc, the Open XML SDK
validator launcher.

## native/core/Cargo.lock

mixdog-ooxml gains: base64 (already a dev edge), flate2, mixdog-rt, mixdog-statefile, reqwest, tar, tokio. New package
entry `tar 0.4.45` (dependencies: filetime, libc) from the local cache. Hakari: include the new edges if regenerated.

## Callers

The Node callers (office verify / document check) take `ensure_ooxml_validator(lane, &Request)` and
`validate_ooxml_schema(lane, path, &Request)` (blocking, from a write-lane job; `Request::new(data_dir)` is download on,
`Microsoft365`); `ValidationResult::to_json()` is Node's result object. The abort flag is an `&AtomicBool`.

## Not compiled

Written without cargo: `cargo test -p mixdog-ooxml --test ooxml_validator_cache` is the first check. The ignored
`live_validator_accepts_blank_documents` downloads and runs the real validator.
